\chapter{The REST Client}

The HTTP layer.  It sends \texttt{Authorization: Bearer} only on keyed
paths, refuses redirects, retries HTTP 429 \texttt{RATE\_LIMITED}, and
does not retry \texttt{MONTHLY\_LIMIT}.  JSON arrays become vectors and
booleans become symbols.  A body with \texttt{success: false} is an
\texttt{api-error} even when the status was 200.

\section{Variables}

\lispVariableSubsection{*api*}

\texttt{https://mcp.thepulse.markets}.  Paths hang off
\texttt{/api/index/v1/}.

\lispVariableSubsection{*api-key*}

The developer key.  On load, the gitignored
\texttt{local-configuration.lisp} file is loaded when it exists
and may rebind this.  Otherwise the library reads
\texttt{PULSE\_API\_KEY}, then
\texttt{THEPULSE\_MARKETS\_API\_KEY}.
The file wins over the environment.  \texttt{use-key} and
\texttt{use-keyless} set it in the image.  Placeholders such as
\texttt{pidx\_your\_key\_here} are treated as no key.

\lispVariableSubsection{*api-cache-timeout-seconds*}

How long \texttt{http-get-json-cached} keeps a response.  Default 60.
Live price calls default to \texttt{:cache nil}.  The cache is
partitioned by a short hash of the key, not by the key itself.

\lispVariableSubsection{*pubkey-cache-timeout-seconds*}

How long \texttt{get-pubkey} keeps the verification ring.  Default 300.

\lispVariableSubsection{*max-retries*}

Attempts for a rate-limited response.  Default 3.  Attempt $n$ waits
$n$ times \texttt{*retry-wait-seconds*} (default 2), or \texttt{Retry-After}
when that header is between 1 and 30 seconds.

\section{Conditions}

All of these are subclasses of \texttt{api-error}.  Readers are
\texttt{api-error-status}, \texttt{api-error-url},
\texttt{api-error-code}, \texttt{api-error-message}, and
\texttt{api-error-body}.

\begin{center}
\begin{tabular}{ll}
\texttt{rate-limited} & HTTP 429, wait and retry \\
\texttt{monthly-limit} & HTTP 429, do not retry \\
\texttt{unauthorized} & HTTP 401 \\
\texttt{plan-restricted} & HTTP 403 \\
\texttt{unsupported-symbol} & the ticker is not served \\
\texttt{service-unavailable} & HTTP 503 \\
\texttt{needs-key} & a keyed call with no usable key \\
\end{tabular}
\end{center}

An unsupported symbol on \texttt{/price} signals.  The same symbol inside
\texttt{get-batch} is one row with \texttt{success} false.  It is not a
price of zero.

\section{Symbols and time}

\lispFunctionSubsection{canonicalize-symbol}

Uppercase a ticker.  \texttt{:btc} and \texttt{"btc"} are both
\texttt{"BTC"}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{canonicalize-symbols}

A symbol, a comma string, or a list.  Duplicates drop, order stays.

\lispFunctionSubsection{canonicalize-interval}

\texttt{1m}, \texttt{5m}, \texttt{1h}, \texttt{1d}.  Short names
\texttt{m}, \texttt{h}, and \texttt{d} map onto those.  The Lisp reader
upcases, so \texttt{:m} and \texttt{:M} are the same symbol and mean a
minute.

\lispFunctionSubsection{canonicalize-time}

An ISO-8601 string passes through.  An integer above $10^{11}$ is UNIX
milliseconds, above $3\cdot10^{9}$ is a universal time, and anything
smaller is UNIX seconds.  The result is \texttt{YYYY-MM-DDTHH:MM:SSZ}.

\lispFunctionSubsection{parse-iso-8601}

The inverse, to universal time.  Fractional seconds are truncated.
\texttt{Z} and numeric offsets are accepted.

\section{Reads}

Each \texttt{get-*} function is the REST path of the same name.
\texttt{get-price} is \texttt{/price} and always requires a key.
\texttt{get-sample} is the keyless BTC, ETH, and SOL print.
\texttt{get-batch} accepts up to 100 symbols.
\texttt{get-print} is the signed print nearest a time, plus
\texttt{deltaMs}.
\texttt{get-history} takes \texttt{:dataset} \texttt{verified} or
\texttt{reconstructed}, an interval, and an optional page
\texttt{:cursor}.
\texttt{get-research-compare} and \texttt{get-source-health} are the
plan-gated research reads.
\texttt{get-verity-price}, \texttt{get-verity-batch}, and
\texttt{get-verity-catalog} are the unsigned breadth surface.
Public, and not sent the key:
\texttt{get-pubkey},
\texttt{get-symbols},
\texttt{get-health},
\texttt{get-status},
\texttt{get-verity-status},
and \texttt{get-verity-venues}.

Results are Yason hash tables.  Pass \texttt{:cache nil} to skip the
cache.  \texttt{get-pubkey} uses its own five-minute cache.
